    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Team Michael Dunne is delighted to present107 Finglas Park, Dublin 11 to the market.\r\nNo. 107 Finglas Park is a charming and well-proportioned mid-terrace family home offering generous living accommodation, excellent storage and a particularly impressive rear garden. The property is ideally suited to first-time buyers, young families or those looking for a home in a mature and established Dublin 11 location.\r\nOn entering the property, you are welcomed by a warm and inviting entrance hallway. To the front is a spacious living room which features a characterful fireplace, creating a comfortable and homely focal point. Double doors lead through to the extended kitchen and dining area, providing a wonderful sense of flow between the living and entertaining spaces.\r\nThe expansive extended kitchen/dining room is undoubtedly one of the highlights of the home. Generous in proportions and flooded with natural light from the Velux roof windows, this is a superb space for everyday family life as well as entertaining. Double doors provide direct access to the substantial rear garden, making it easy to enjoy the outdoor space during the warmer months. The garden is a fantastic feature of the property and also benefits from a large block-built shed, which is insulated and fitted with electricity, offering excellent flexibility as a workshop, home office, hobby room or additional storage.\r\nUpstairs, there are two well-proportioned double bedrooms, both benefiting from useful storage, together with a family bathroom. The converted attic provides a valuable third bedroom and is enhanced by a bay window overlooking the rear garden, creating a bright and pleasant additional living space.\r\nTo the front, the property benefits from off-street parking, while the generous rear garden provides a rare amount of outdoor space for a home of this type.\r\nFinglas Park is situated in a mature and well-established residential area of Dublin 11, with an excellent range of amenities close by. The property is within easy reach of Finglas Village, where residents can access a variety of shops, cafés and local services, while Finglas Village Centre provides further retail and everyday conveniences. Charlestown Shopping Centre is also nearby, offering a wide selection of shops and services, with IKEA and Clearwater Shopping Centre also within easy reach. \r\nThe area is particularly well catered for in terms of education, with a broad selection of primary and secondary schools in Finglas and the surrounding areas, including St Canice's, Finglas Parochial National School, New Cross College, Beneavin De La Salle College and St Michael's Holy Faith Secondary School. \r\nFor those who enjoy the outdoors, there is an excellent choice of parks, green spaces and sporting facilities nearby, including Tolka Valley Park, Mellowes Park, Johnstown Park and Farnham Park, while a wide range of local sporting clubs and leisure facilities cater for football, GAA, fitness and other activities. \r\nThe property also benefits from excellent transport links, with numerous Dublin Bus routes serving the area and providing access towards Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. The M50 and M1 are readily accessible by car, while Dublin Airport is also within convenient driving distance. The location further benefits from Finglas's proximity to the Royal Canal and Tolka Valley Greenway, providing attractive options for walking and cycling. \r\nOverall, No. 107 Finglas Park is a superb opportunity to acquire a spacious three-bedroom home with a fantastic extended kitchen/dining area, generous gardens, an insulated block-built shed and off-street parking, all set within a mature and highly convenient Dublin 11 location.\r\n\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
